Rights Department, Accounts Payable,

Q2 2027 FOREIGN ROYALTIES STATEMENT
RLS-2027-Q2-0417.

The Q2 foreign-rights royalty statement for
your authors' translated editions is
finalized at EUR 12,844.50, payable to your
standing account on the normal cycle. One
document action is attached: the W-8BEN
renewal.

1. STATEMENT SUMMARY (RLS-2027-Q2-0417)

  Territory group:   German + Dutch
                    translations
  Royalty basis:     6% net on
                    41,200 units
  Gross royalties:   EUR 14,935.40
  Withholding (DTA
  applied):          -EUR 2,090.90
  ---------------------------------------
  Net payable:       EUR 12,844.50
  Disbursement:      July 20, to the
                    IBAN on file
                    (unchanged since
                    2022)

2. HOW ROYALTIES PAY (STANDING
   ARRANGEMENT)

    1. The statement and the
       unit counts are in your
       rights-management portal
       (type the address
       yourself) - compare
       there, not against
       email summaries.
    2. Payment goes to the
       IBAN on file - the
       same account every
       cycle since 2022.
       Bank-detail changes
       are made by signed
       letter on your
       letterhead, confirmed
       by a callback to your
       agency's registered
       number, then held for
       one full cycle before
       first payment (a
       fraud-control cooling
       period written into
       the agency agreement,
       clause 14).
    3. The W-8BEN renewal
       (signed and scanned)
       goes to your rights
       manager by the
       portal's document
       upload - one form,
       no fees, no SMS
       codes.

  RightsLink will NEVER:
  - Announce a per-cycle
    "disbursement account
    re-verification"
    collecting IBAN +
    SWIFT + signatory
    specimen + mobile SMS
    code by email (the
    specimen-plus-SMS
    package against a
    lookalike domain is
    precisely how royalty
    interception happens;
    real payment platforms
    verify beneficiaries
    with the receiving
    bank, not by emailing
    payees)
  - Roll payments to
    "Q3 (October)" for
    missing an emailed
    re-verification (the
    only thing that delays
    payment is a payee-side
    document like the
    W-8BEN, and only the
    withholding is affected
    - net royalties accrue)
  - Use lookalike domains
    such as
    "rightslink-agency"
    or "rl-disbursement"

3. VERIFY THIS NOTICE

  - Statement and unit
    counts in the rights
    portal (typed address)
  - Your rights manager's
    address is on prior
    correspondence you
    initiated
  - Report lookalike
    royalty notices to
